---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/nav.astro";
import Home from "../components/home.astro";
import Tech from "../components/tech.astro";
import Projects from "../components/projects.astro";
import Contact from "../components/contact.astro";
import Career from "../components/career.astro";
import localData from '../data/home.json';

interface ProfileData {
  webpageTitle: string;
}

const isApiLive = import.meta.env.PROD; // Auto true in production
const BASE_URL = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL;

let data: ProfileData; // data as ProfileData

if (isApiLive && BASE_URL) {
  try {
    const response = await fetch(`${BASE_URL}/home`);
    if (!response.ok) throw new Error('Network response was not ok');
    data = await response.json();
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("API Fetch failed, falling back to mock data", error);
    data = localData as ProfileData;
  }
} else {
  data = localData as ProfileData;
}

const { webpageTitle } = data;
---

<Layout title={webpageTitle}>
  <section class="content-pack-homepage space-y-10">
    <header class="max-w-3xl space-y-4">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-accent">Featured resource</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold leading-tight md:text-5xl text-base-content">Service Page Strategy Guide</h1>
      <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-base-content/80">Explain the core principles of service page strategy for client success teams improving activation in Toronto.</p>
    </header>

    <nav class="space-y-3" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-base-content">Table of contents</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-base-content/80">
        <li><a href="#what-service-page-strategy-means-for-client-success-teams">What service page strategy means for client success teams</a></li>
        <li><a href="#what-this-site-covers">What this site covers</a></li>
        <li><a href="#main-framework-and-checklist">Main framework and checklist</a></li>
        <li><a href="#key-subtopics">Key subtopics</a></li>
        <li><a href="#faq">FAQ</a></li>
        <li><a href="#methodology-and-trust">Methodology and trust</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>
    <div class="grid gap-8">
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 id="what-service-page-strategy-means-for-client-success-teams" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-base-content">What service page strategy means for client success teams</h2>
        <p class="text-base-content/80">Service page strategy is the blueprint that guides client success teams in Toronto through the process of creating, maintaining, and optimizing service pages. It ensures that these pages effectively communicate the value of your services to potential clients, driving activation and conversions.</p>
        <p class="text-base-content/80">For client success teams, a well-defined service page strategy means clearer handoffs, reduced rework, and more consistent outcomes. It helps teams work more efficiently, meet client expectations, and ultimately drive business growth.</p>
        <p class="text-base-content/80">Key entities and topics covered in service page strategy include service offerings, target audience, unique value propositions, content creation, SEO, and performance metrics.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 id="what-this-site-covers" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-base-content">What this site covers</h2>
        <p class="text-base-content/80">This guide takes a practical, Toronto-focused approach to service page strategy. It&#39;s designed for client success teams looking to improve activation and drive results. The tone is clear and concise, focusing on actionable steps and real-world examples.</p>
        <p class="text-base-content/80">We cover the core principles of service page strategy, common risks, and metrics to measure after changes. We also delve into key subtopics and provide a methodology section to build trust in our advice.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 id="main-framework-and-checklist" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-base-content">Main framework and checklist</h2>
        <p class="text-base-content/80">Our main framework for service page strategy consists of five key steps: Define, Plan, Create, Optimize, and Measure. Let&#39;s dive into each step and the practical checks involved.</p>
        <p class="text-base-content/80">1. **Define**: Clearly outline your service offerings, target audience, and unique value propositions. Confirm the owner of the strategy and the required inputs and expected outcomes.</p>
        <p class="text-base-content/80">2. **Plan**: Develop a content plan that aligns with your target audience&#39;s needs and search intent. Identify the decision criteria and the first metric that will show the strategy is working.</p>
        <p class="text-base-content/80">3. **Create**: Craft compelling, SEO-optimized content that highlights your services&#39; benefits and addresses client pain points. Ensure the content is accurate, up-to-date, and consistent with your brand voice.</p>
        <p class="text-base-content/80">4. **Optimize**: Continuously improve your service pages based on performance data, user feedback, and changes in the market. Regularly review and update your strategy to ensure it remains relevant and effective.</p>
        <p class="text-base-content/80">5. **Measure**: Track key performance indicators (KPIs) to assess the success of your service page strategy. Use these metrics to inform future optimizations and ensure your strategy is driving activation and conversions.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 id="key-subtopics" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-base-content">Key subtopics</h2>
        <p class="text-base-content/80">In addition to our main framework, we cover several key subtopics to help you refine your service page strategy. These include service page workflow, best practices, FAQs, glossary, checklist, and methodology.</p>
        <p class="text-base-content/80">Each subtopic fits into our main framework, providing deeper insights and practical tools to help you implement and optimize your service page strategy.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 id="faq" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-base-content">FAQ</h2>
        <p class="text-base-content/80">Our FAQ section addresses common questions about service page strategy. It provides quick answers to help you understand and implement the strategy more effectively.</p>
        <p class="text-base-content/80">Use the answers in practice by applying them to your specific situation. If you have additional questions, don&#39;t hesitate to reach out to our team for personalized advice.</p>
      </section>
      <section class="space-y-3">
        <h2 id="methodology-and-trust" class="text-2xl font-semibold text-base-content">Methodology and trust</h2>
        <p class="text-base-content/80">Our methodology is built on extensive research, industry best practices, and real-world testing. We&#39;ve drawn from trusted sources such as Google, Moz, and leading marketing experts to ensure our advice is reliable and effective.</p>
        <p class="text-base-content/80">We&#39;re committed to maintaining the highest standards of accuracy and integrity. Our team regularly reviews and updates the guide to ensure it remains relevant and valuable to our readers.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <section class="space-y-3">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-base-content">Related links</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-base-content/80">
        <li><a href="https://protonbraulio.github.io/lt-20260522-042729105-career-portfolio-01-9105-92bdb5ea/service-page-strategy-workflow">Service Page Strategy Workflow</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://protonbraulio.github.io/lt-20260522-042729105-career-portfolio-01-9105-92bdb5ea/service-page-strategy-best-practices">Service Page Strategy Best Practices</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://protonbraulio.github.io/lt-20260522-042729105-career-portfolio-01-9105-92bdb5ea/service-page-strategy-faq">Service Page Strategy FAQ</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://protonbraulio.github.io/lt-20260522-042729105-career-portfolio-01-9105-92bdb5ea/service-page-strategy-glossary">Service Page Strategy Glossary</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://protonbraulio.github.io/lt-20260522-042729105-career-portfolio-01-9105-92bdb5ea/service-page-strategy-checklist">Service Page Strategy Checklist</a></li>
        <li><a href="https://protonbraulio.github.io/lt-20260522-042729105-career-portfolio-01-9105-92bdb5ea/service-page-strategy-methodology">Service Page Strategy Methodology</a></li>
      </ul>
    </section>
    <div class="rounded border p-6 border-accent/20">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-base-content">Next step</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base-content/80">Talk to Career Portfolio Load Test 01 20260522-042729105 about service page strategy.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
